
# --- Forecastle: Castle integration (generated, do not edit) ---
#
# Nothing to do on a normal start.
#
# This fragment used to run a preboot VM on every start, daemon and eval, to
# expand build.config into sys.config and to create releases/RELEASES. Both are
# gone. Mix writes the sys.config its own launcher boots from and expands
# runtime configuration in the booting VM, exactly as it does for a release
# Forecastle was never involved in - which is also why the launcher's own
# defaults no longer have to be applied here, since it assigns them itself
# before anything reads them. RELEASES is created by bin/castle, ahead of the
# operation that first needs it.
#
# The hook is kept, and still appended after any env.sh the project supplied,
# because a normal start is not the only start there is. A relup that restarts
# the emulator has release_handler write its provisional target to
# releases/new_start_erl.data and deliberately leave releases/start_erl.data
# pointing at the permanent version, so that a crash before commit rolls back -
# and the stock launcher knows nothing about that file. Consuming that marker
# and re-execing the launcher is this hook's remaining job, and doing nothing
# here on an ordinary start is what leaves room for it. See
# https://github.com/ausimian/forecastle/issues/10.
# --- Forecastle: end Castle integration ---
